Description: Fix the SQLITE_ALLOW_ROWID_IN_VIEW bug-compatibility option
 When SQLite is built with SQLITE_ALLOW_ROWID_IN_VIEW, a subquery keeps a
 visible rowid, so selectExpander() adds one more result column for a
 nested parenthesized join than the subquery's result list holds. It then
 copies the name of that column from past the end of the list, and name
 resolution dereferences the garbage pointer in sqlite3MatchEName().
 .
 This backport of upstream check-in 7a3d0027f8 leaves out the new
 SQLITE_CONFIG_ROWID_IN_VIEW sqlite3_config() verb, the -no-rowid-in-view
 shell option and the ALLOW_ROWID_IN_VIEW entry in PRAGMA compile_options.
 Without the verb, ViewCanHaveRowid is always true under
 SQLITE_ALLOW_ROWID_IN_VIEW, which is the upstream default.
Origin: backport, https://sqlite.org/src/info/7a3d0027f81e8def
Author: drh <drh@sqlite.org>
Bug-Ubuntu: https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/sqlite3/+bug/2087772
Applied-Upstream: 3.45.3, https://github.com/sqlite/sqlite/commit/74851f66811854c772a9b2d0a13f1e9e82b69c25
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-09-23

